<title>SRI LANKA: Sri Lanka 1997 wheat imports seen at 750,000 T.</title>
<headline>Sri Lanka 1997 wheat imports seen at 750,000 T.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sri Lanka's wheat imports in 1997 are seen at about 750,000 tonnes, lower than last year's nearly a million tonnes, a top finance ministry official said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>P.B, Jayasundera, deputy secretary of Treasury, told Reuters in an interview that anticipated lower imports this year were mostly due to increased demand for rice, led by a slashing in the wheat subsidy.</p>
</text>
